    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="0849" n="735" xml:id="pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.156/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at
                        Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Denning</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-09T19:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:10
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Announcement made in morning press that port adjudication to be postponed for a
                    short time.</p>
                <p>I am reliably informed that the French diplomatic agent was instructed by his
                    Government on November 6 to notify the representative of the Sultan at Tangier,
                    who is the President of the Adjudication Commission, to postpone the port
                    concession until further notice. There was no explanation.</p>
                <p>The British agent also received a telegram which stated that Poincaré had agreed
                    to postpone the port adjudication until after the Lausanne conference as a
                    result of Lord Curzon’s personal plea.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Denning</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
